      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Punks, sex workers and society in transition: documenting postwar Japan – in pictures"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A Long Shadow: Postwar Japan Through the Lens will be the first show of Japanese photography in more than three decades at New York’s Metropolitan Museum of Art. The exhibit brings together 15 intergenerational artists as well as photographic prints, including more than 25 books and magazines and a video installation, all combining to show how photographers in Japan documented the country in the decades after the second world war. The exhibition runs until 2 May 2027",
